[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Best Art Critics]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.99]Who is the student's best critic? | 谁是这位学生最好的评论家？
[00:15.97]I am an art student and I paint a lot of pictures. | 我是个学艺术的学生，画了很多画。
[00:21.45]Many people pretend that they understand modern art. | 很多人假装懂得现代艺术。
[00:26.32]They always tell you what a picture is 'about'. | 他们总是告诉你一幅画的“意思”是什么。
[00:30.55]Of course, many pictures are not 'about' anything. | 当然，很多画并不是“表现”什么，
[00:35.30]They are just pretty patterns. | 它们只是漂亮的图案。
[00:38.11]We like them in the same way that we like pretty curtain material. | 我们喜爱它们就像我们喜欢漂亮的窗帘布料一样。
[00:44.18]I think that young children often appreciate modern pictures better than anyone else. | 我认为小孩子们往往比任何人都更能欣赏现代绘画。
[00:52.01]They notice more. | 他们观察到的东西更多。
[00:54.27]My sister is only seven, | 我妹妹只有7岁，
[00:57.08]but she always tells me whether my pictures are good or not. | 但她总能说出我的画是好还是糟。
[01:02.67]She came into my room yesterday. | 昨天她到我房里来了。
[01:05.94]'What are you doing?' she asked. | “你在干什么？”她问。
[01:09.36]'I'm hanging this picture on the wall,' I answered. 'It's a new one. Do you like it?' | “我正把这幅画挂到墙上去，”我回答说，“这是幅新画，你喜欢吗？”
[01:17.48]She looked at it critically for a moment. | 她用挑剔的目光看了一会儿。
[01:21.07]'It's all right,' she said, 'but isn't it upside down?' | “还可以吧，”她说，“不过是不是挂倒了？”
[01:26.93]I looked at it again. | 我又看了一下。
[01:28.97]She was right! It was! | 她说对了！是挂倒了！
